T* (devotion and brotherhood. Yet love proved mightier than death. The postal clerks of America refused to let their companion) Tj
T* (fade into the dust of an unmarked grave. Every dime and dollar poured into his memorial was a declaration that loyalty,) Tj
T* (courage, and unconditional friendship are eternal.") Tj
ET
BT
/F9 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.098 g
54. 623.5 Td
(Patrick Callahan looked through the glass of the memorial case with moist eyes: "You’re home now, Owney. No more frozen) Tj
T* (switches, no more rough boxcars, no more hurried transfers in the middle of the night. You’ve got the best run of all) Tj
T* (now—standing in the nation’s capital, where every child who loves trains and dogs can come see what true loyalty looks) Tj
T* (like.") Tj
ET
BT
/F9 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.098 g
54. 559.5 Td
(The Chief Curator of the Postal Museum pointed to the gleaming medals: "Here are one thousand and seventeen pieces of) Tj
T* (metal. Each one tells a story of an American city in the golden age of steam. But more than that, they tell the story of a stray) Tj
T* (dog who found a purpose, found a family, and became the heart of a nation.") Tj
ET
BT
/F9 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.098 g
54. 509. Td
(Owney said, "In the quiet halls of memory, the bright, brave bark of the terrier from Albany echoes across the centuries, as) Tj
T* (timeless as the click of the rails and the song of the open road.") Tj
ET
BT
/F9 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.098 g
54. 472. Td
(Golden sunlight streams through the high windows of the Smithsonian museum rotunda. Visitors from every continent gaze) Tj
T* (upon the beloved terrier in his medal-studded harness, smiling with wonder at the legendary mascot of the United States) Tj
T* (Railway Mail.) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 10 Tf
11.5 TL
