54. 421.5 Td
(1904. St. Louis World’s Fair \(Louisiana Purchase Exposition\). The massive neoclassical United States Government Pavilion.) Tj
T* (Millions of visitors from around the world file past the central exhibition case.) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.098 g
54. 384.5 Td
(The Director addressed the gathered crowd: "Here stands Owney, who carried the American spirit to Japan, China, the Suez,) Tj
T* (and across one hundred and forty thousand miles of rails. He represents the miracle of American communications—the) Tj
T* (system that unites eighty million citizens from ocean to ocean.") Tj
ET
BT
/F9 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.098 g
54. 334. Td
(The Historian narrated: "At the World's Fair, international diplomats who had greeted Owney in Yokohama and Shanghai) Tj
T* (came to pay homage. Following the exposition, the Post Office Department officially transferred Owney to the permanent) Tj
T* (custody of the Smithsonian Institution in Washington, D.C.") Tj
ET
BT
/F9 10 Tf
11.5 TL
